{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ emotional emotions psychologically psychological) (+ effects impact affect affects))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_318853832#5_734634698","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2650","rank":2,"snippet":"Watch Annular Solar Eclipse June 2020: Date, Timings, Effects, And Where To Watch An annular solar eclipse is set to occur on June 21, 2020. Here’s all you need to know about the June 2020 solar eclipse timings, effects, and precautions. Solar Eclipse June 2020; Explained Effect of Solar Eclipse: Precautions for June 2020 Solar Eclipse: Image Source: Shutterstock Video unavailable SUBSCRIBE TO US WATCH US LIVE \" , \"segment\": \"Further, it is also believed that astrological changes occur due to solar eclipses. Here are some effects of a solar eclipse on the human body: 1. You may feel dizzy or tired during a solar eclipse. It may also interfere with decision-making. 2. The digestive system might be affected. 3. A <cover>solar eclipse might also have psychological effects. </cover>One might be agitated or even have unusual dreams during this period.\" , \"start_char\": 1774.000000 , \"title\": \"Annular Solar Eclipse June 2020: Date, timings, effects, and where to watch\" , \"url\": \"https://www.republicworld.com/technology-news/science/solar-eclipse-june-2020-date-time-and-effects.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_318853832#6_734635937","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"8/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_318853832#5_734634698","relevance":2,"reason":"This is the same Republic World solar-eclipse effects article seen earlier, with a direct but brief claim that a solar eclipse might have psychological effects such as agitation and unusual dreams. It is not dedicated to mental health and the evidence is thin/popular rather than well-supported.","learned":"Republic World repeats the claim that solar eclipses may cause dizziness/tiredness, interfere with decision-making, and have psychological effects such as agitation or unusual dreams."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ brain psychological mental) (+ awe anxiety stress mood emotions))","reason":"Search for psychologically focused explanations of solar eclipses, including brain, awe, anxiety, stress, mood, or emotional effects, which may yield more dedicated mental-health evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ brain psychological mental) (+ awe anxiety stress mood emotions))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1756349705#3_3505966732","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2651","rank":1,"snippet":"comes about because of using the general term ‘solar eclipse’ to describe both the total phase when the sun disk is completely blocked, and the minutes before and after totality when there is still some of the sun’s disk visible. It is harmful to view even a sliver of the sun disk because of its intensity, and so to simply say that you should not view a solar eclipse is rather inaccurate. Do lunar and solar eclipses have any noticeable effect on humans? There is no evidence that eclipses have any physical effect on humans. However, eclipses have always been capable of producing profound psychological effects. For millennia, solar eclipses have been interpreted as portents of doom by virtually every known civilization. These have stimulated responses that run the gamut from human sacrifices to feelings of <cover>awe and bewilderment. Although there are no direct physical effects involving known forces, the consequences of the induced human psychological states have indeed led to physical effects.\" , \"start_char\": 2108.000000 , \"title\": \"FAQ | Total Solar Eclipse </cover>2017\" , \"url\": \"https://eclipse2017.nasa.gov/faq\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"9/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1756349705#3_3505966732","relevance":2,"reason":"NASA's eclipse FAQ directly answers that eclipses have no known physical effects on humans but can produce profound psychological effects, including awe, bewilderment, and doom-related interpretations. It is authoritative and useful, but it is an eclipse FAQ rather than a document dedicated specifically to mental health effects.","learned":"NASA states that solar/lunar eclipses have no known physical effects on humans but can produce profound psychological effects, historically ranging from awe and bewilderment to doom interpretations."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" \"profound psychological effects\")","reason":"Follow the authoritative NASA wording to find other documents or fuller passages directly about psychological effects of solar eclipses."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" \"profound psychological effects\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1756349705#4_3505968220","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2652","rank":2,"snippet":"<cover>profound psychological effects. For millennia, solar eclipses have been interpreted as portents of doom by virtually every known civilization. These have stimulated responses that run the gamut from human sacrifices to feelings of awe and bewilderment. Although there are no direct physical effects involving known forces, the consequences of the induced human psychological states have indeed led to physical effects. How are eyes damaged by staring at the sun? Solar retinopathy is a result of too much ultraviolet light flooding the retina. In extreme cases this can cause blindness, but is so painful that it is rare for someone to be able to stare at the sun for that long. Typically, eye damage from staring at the sun results in blurred vision, dark or yellow spots, pain in bright light or loss of vision in the center of the eye (the fovea). Permanent damage to the retina has been shown to occur in ~100 seconds, but the exact time before damage occurs will vary with the intensity of the sun on a particular day and with how much the viewer's pupil is dilated from decongestants and other drugs they may be taking.\" , \"start_char\":</cover>","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1756349705#3_3505966732","rank":1,"relevance":2}]}}
{"request":{"judgments":"10/50"}}
