{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_750852180#5_1356467592","relevance":2,"reason":"The article is about Nebraska villages preparing for the 2017 total solar eclipse and includes direct support that viewing an eclipse can be life-changing, socially bonding, and can trigger a 'primal fear.' However, mental health or psychological effects are not the central focus.","learned":"Eclipse viewers may experience camaraderie, a life-changing sense of awe, and even primal fear despite intellectually understanding the event."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ \"mental state\" \"state of mind\" \"human behavior\" behavioral psychological) (+ affect effects impact))","reason":"Search for more focused documents discussing solar eclipses' effects on mental state, behavior, or psychology, which may yield grade-3 evidence dedicated to mental-health-relevant impacts."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ \"mental state\" \"state of mind\" \"human behavior\" behavioral psychological) (+ affect effects impact))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_584664443#7_1333606530","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2673","rank":5,"snippet":"Myths and Superstitions Around Solar Eclipses June 10: Annular Solar Eclipse Watch both eclipses LIVE Why are the two eclipses noteworthy? Ancient Explanations for Solar Eclipse Hungry Demons, Thieving Dogs Native American Solar Eclipse Myths and Legends Angry Sun How superstition influenced the course of history Quarreling Sun and Moon Modern Day Sun Superstitions No Scientific Basis Make your own pinhole projector \" , \"segment\": \"Not all superstitions surrounding solar eclipses are about doom. In Italy, for example, it is believed that flowers planted during a solar eclipse are brighter and more colorful than flowers planted any other time of the year. No Scientific Basis Scientists and astronomers around the world have debunked any such claims. There is no scientific evidence that solar eclipses can <cover>affect human behavior, health, or the environment. Scientists, however, do emphasize that anyone watching a solar eclipse </cover>must protect their eyes. Make your own pinhole projector Topics: Astronomy, Eclipses, Moon, Sun\" , \"start_char\": 4126.000000 , \"title\": \"Solar Eclipse Myths and Superstitions\" , \"url\": \"https://www.timeanddate.com/eclipse/solar-eclipse-myths.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_318853832#6_734635937","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_318853832#5_734634698","rank":2,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_386975294#5_843851629","rank":3,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1756349705#3_3505966732","rank":4,"relevance":2}]}}
