{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ \"mental effects\" \"psychological effects\" \"psychological impact\" \"effect on humans\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_37_1386631282#2_3072253497","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2677","rank":1,"snippet":"1_doc_37_1386631282#2_3072253497\" , \"end_char\": 2093.000000 , \"headings\": \"Difference Between Solar Eclipse and Lunar Eclipse Difference Between Solar Eclipse and Lunar Eclipse Main Difference Solar Eclipse vs. Lunar Eclipse Comparison Chart What is the Solar Eclipse? What is Lunar Eclipse? Key Differences Conclusion Harlon Moss \" , \"segment\": \"Watching a solar eclipse without sunglasses protection can seriously harm your eyesight while It is quite safe to view a lunar eclipse by the naked eye. A <cover>solar eclipse has consistently had a more intense effect on humans </cover>than a lunar eclipse. Comparison Chart Solar Eclipse Lunar Eclipse A solar eclipse is the one in which the sun blocked by the moon. Lunar eclipse mentions to the eclipse in which the Moon appears dim, as it passes into Earth shadow. Cause Moon is blocking the Sun. Moon takes on the shadow of the Earth. When Do You See It Depending on where you are, usually, the eclipse is seen earlier in the west. Everywhere at the same time. Frequency Once in every eighteen months. Twice a year Position The moon lies between the "}}
