{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"solar eclipse\" (+ \"affect mental health\" \"affects mental health\" \"impact mental health\" \"impacts mental health\" \"mental health impact\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_50_1755625459#11_2543173682","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2703","rank":1,"snippet":"orange and red) in the morning and in the sunset. As more moisture, smoke and other dust particles are there in the atmosphere of the earth in the evening than in the morning, red colour can only reach our eyes during the sunset, so the sky appears reddish then. But in the morning, even the yellow colour can reach us as there is less chance of scattering than in the evening, so the sky appears yellowish. Thanks. Arun K's answer to Why is the sky blue? Arun K's answer to What occurs during a <cover>solar eclipse? Arun K's answer to Does full moon affect mental health? </cover>Does it have any power? Quora User , B.E. Mechanical Engineering Answered 4 years ago · Author has 76 answers and 102.2K answer views This goes down to the basics of light in physics.\" , \"start_char\": 6424.000000 , \"title\": \"What is reason for a red sun in the morning and the evening? - Quora\" , \"url\": \"https://www.quora.com/What-is-reason-for-a-red-sun-in-the-morning-and-the-evening\" }"}}
